<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21298] sanity-pcc test_204a: pin xattr unsupported in b2_16 interop</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21298</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/68b0a330-a94a-4e88-bfc5-2dcecfd1122f" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/68b0a330-a94a-4e88-bfc5-2dcecfd1122f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_204a failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;failed to pcc pin /mnt/lustre/f204a.sanity-pcc.dat
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Interop&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4774" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4774&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 7.0.0-22-generic&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.16.1.2&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: b2_16&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-b2_16/6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-b2_16/6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 5.14.0-427.31.1_lustre.el9.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Filed by Patch Watcher's weekly branch filer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-pcc test_204a fails at lfs pcc pin -i 2. The test log reports "cannot read or parse pin xattr" and "Operation not supported (95)". Backend setup and file creation complete before this command.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow, 2026-10-25 through 2026-11-23: 78 failed branch sessions, first seen October 29, latest November 22. Trigger jobs: lustre-master (36/533 suite runs, 6.75%) and lustre-master-next (42/623, 6.74%). The failing code-branch/config rows are b2_16, full-part-2: 36/36 and 42/42 runs fail. Master/master-next code rows pass. The suite-wide percentages include configurations that do not fail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/68b0a330-a94a-4e88-bfc5-2dcecfd1122f" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/68b0a330-a94a-4e88-bfc5-2dcecfd1122f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d2b42494-b671-4951-9fc2-63184c135515" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d2b42494-b671-4951-9fc2-63184c135515&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test log: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/e971ae88-a5f4-45d7-b6f8-e2d61bc673ca/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/e971ae88-a5f4-45d7-b6f8-e2d61bc673ca/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This points to a missing interop prerequisite or version guard for pin-xattr support. The exact client/server split needs confirmation. No local reproduction was attempted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LU searches for test_204a, pcc pin, and pin xattr found feature tickets &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10499" title="Readonly Persistent Client Cache support" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10499"&gt;LU-10499&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19712" title="Add ability for admins to pin files into Pool" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19712"&gt;LU-19712&lt;/a&gt;, but no ticket for this recurring interop test failure. Open change 57671 adds tests 204d/204e and does not guard test_204a. EX cannot be searched with this account, so an EX duplicate could not be ruled out.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
